<h1>unranking</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Given a ranking, r, generate the r<sup>th</sup> <a href="permutation.html"><em>permutation</em></a> of n elements.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
This can be done in O(n) time.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="http://antoinecomeau.blogspot.com/2014/07/mapping-between-permutations-and.html" target="_blank">(C)</a>. <a href="http://www.davdata.nl/math/ranks.html" target="_blank">(Delphi?)</a>. <strong>Wendy Myrvold and Frank Ruskey</strong>, <em>Ranking and Unranking Permutations in Linear Time</em>, 13 April 2000, give <a href="http://webhome.cs.uvic.ca/~ruskey/Publications/RankPerm/RankPerm.html" target="_blank">linear time ranking and unranking algorithms</a>.

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

